.. rubric:: Port and outputs

The source automatically writes ``/tls/tlN`` in creation order, or
``/subgrids/<subgrid ID>/tls/tlN`` for a CPU or CUDA HSG source. ``Vinc`` and
``Vtotal`` are incident and total line voltages (V); ``Iinc`` and ``Itotal``
are line currents (A). These are terminal quantities, not a point receiver's
local electric/magnetic fields. The line resistance is the reference impedance.

``frequency``, ``S11``, ``Zin``, ``Yin`` and their validity masks are already
calculated. ``Zin_current`` is an independent current-wave de-embedding check;
do not reconstruct it by simply dividing raw staggered histories. Use
``python -m gprMax.toolboxes.Plotting.plot_port model.h5 --port tls/tl1 --save``
to inspect the stored result and its timing. See :ref:`tl-port-output` for
the line's spatial/temporal reference plane and masks, and :ref:`study-source`
for changing generator drives while retaining the passive line termination.
